  "hypothesis": "On the bounded search the optimizer basins are real optima, so one chain per basin (within 20 nats) surfaces basin disagreement as an rhat failure without hurting the fits that have a single basin.",
  "reason": "Fair retest of chain_init map_basins after 988826 refuted it on the legacy unbounded search; detector for the two-rotation-mode class (g8_r90).",
  "conclusion": "REFUTED as a default. 21/32 fits report 2-5 basins after the bounded search; 12 have a second basin within the 20-nat margin and got a chain there; 11 escalations (robust 2), 9 final gate failures (rhat 1.06-2.7, min ESS 2-28), sum wall 1.58x, sum steps 1.45x; fits with one basin unchanged (per-fit steps median 1.03x). The failing chains sit in basins 3-20 nats below the MAP (posterior mass e^-3 to e^-20): NUTS does not leave them in 500 draws, so the rhat failure measures the trap, not the posterior. Basins within 3 nats: 3 fits (g8_r90 0.14, g13_r90 1.6, g2_r90 1.7), of which only g2_r90 escalated; g8_r90 (the genuinely ambiguous rotation) passed at rhat 1.02 with theta between the two modes. map_basin_margin is the useful product: the same column in the map_jitter reference already identifies the 3 fits, so the census flags margin < 3 nats without starting chains there. A margin-3 twin would be the honest mixture test if ever needed.",
